---
/**
 * PHASE R — the hub page, rebuilt in vertical slices from the approved
 * wireframe. This file is reduced to the slice that has actually been
 * built and reviewed. Slices R2-R11 add one section each.
 *
 *   R1       Cover               <- shipped
 *   R2       About               <- shipped
 *   R-shell  Collapse bands      <- shipped (four bands, 8-col tablet step)
 *   R3       Educational Leader  <- shipped
 *   R4       Premier Leadership  <- shipped (batched with R5)
 *   R5       Everyday Legends    <- shipped
 *   R4.2     Premier corrections <- shipped
 *   R6       Athletic Management <- shipped
 *   R7       Feature Quote       <- shipped
 *   R8       Index               <- shipped
 *   R9       Charging It         <- shipped
 *   R10      Contact + footer    <- shipped
 *   R12      Folio marginalia    <- THIS SLICE
 *
 *   R11 /privacy
 *
 * R4 AND R5 ARE THE ONLY PAIR BATCHED IN THE WHOLE REBUILD. They are
 * built to rhyme and the failure mode of a rhyme is a repeat, so they
 * had to be reviewed side by side. Everything after this returns to
 * one slice at a time.
 *
 * Every component from the old build is still on disk in
 * src/components/ — nothing was deleted. They are simply not imported.
 * That now includes ContactSection.astro and Footer.astro: R10's
 * Contact.astro PORTS the Phase F form out of the first (the markup,
 * the four states, the honeypot, the Turnstile mount and the whole
 * script, carried across unedited) into the rebuilt grid, and
 * PageFooter.astro replaces the second, which hung on .spread and
 * .col-trim and drew its rule with a token R1 deleted.
 *
 * THE TEN-<h2> STRUCTURE CLOSES AT 10 OF 10 WITH THIS SLICE. Portrait
 * (hidden), About (hidden), Educational Leader, Premier Leadership,
 * Everyday Legends Foundation, Athletic Management, the pull quote,
 * Index (hidden), Charging It to the Game, Contact.
 *
 * THE FOLIO SITS OUTSIDE <main> AND OUTSIDE <footer>, LAST IN THE
 * DOCUMENT. It is position:fixed, pointer-events:none and aria-hidden,
 * so it is neither a section nor content: it has no entry in
 * src/data/sections.ts, no <h2>, and it takes no part in the
 * ten-<h2> structure. Mounted last so it cannot sit between the
 * landmarks, and because nothing in the page depends on it existing.
 *
 * IT CARRIES THE PAGE'S ONLY SCROLL LISTENER. Before R12 the build had
 * zero, and CONTEXT.md's "one scroll listener exists in the entire
 * build" described something that was not true yet. A second one is
 * not to be added; a future component that needs scroll reuses this.
 *
 * THE FOOTER SITS OUTSIDE <main>. A <footer> nested inside <main> is
 * a generic element and resolves to no landmark; outside it, it is
 * the contentinfo landmark. It is not a section, carries no <h2> and
 * has no entry in src/data/sections.ts.
 *
 * NO ANCESTOR OF A SECTION CARRIES A MAX-WIDTH, A CENTRING
 * margin-inline, OR A CONTAINER WRAPPER. <main> is a bare element.
 * That is the rule this rebuild exists to enforce: a single max-width
 * above a section collapses every column placement below it and
 * produces the centred stack that cost three passes.
 *
 * <main> also carries no transform, opacity, filter or isolation, so a
 * descendant's mix-blend-mode composites against the page ground.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Cover from '../components/Cover.astro';
import About from '../components/About.astro';
import EducationalLeader from '../components/EducationalLeader.astro';
import PremierLeadership from '../components/PremierLeadership.astro';
import EverydayLegends from '../components/EverydayLegends.astro';
import AthleticManagement from '../components/AthleticManagement.astro';
import FeatureQuote from '../components/FeatureQuote.astro';
import Index from '../components/Index.astro';
import ChargingItToTheGame from '../components/ChargingItToTheGame.astro';
import Contact from '../components/Contact.astro';
import PageFooter from '../components/PageFooter.astro';
import FolioMarginalia from '../components/FolioMarginalia.astro';
import Masthead from '../components/Masthead.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Dr. Syreeta McClain — Where Leadership Meets Legacy">
  {/* R16. MOUNTED BEFORE <main>, unlike the folio. It is site chrome
      that sits at the top of the viewport, so DOM order, visual order
      and tab order agree; and its one link reaches the tab order
      before the page's content rather than after the footer. It is
      display:none by default and position:fixed when it renders, so it
      contributes no layout in either state and mounting it here costs
      <main> nothing. It carries NO SCRIPT — the folio's own history of
      being mounted before <main> and capturing an empty section list
      does not apply, because there is nothing here to capture. */}
  <Masthead />

  <main id="main">
    <Cover />
    <About />
    <EducationalLeader />
    <PremierLeadership />
    <EverydayLegends />
    <AthleticManagement />
    <FeatureQuote />
    <Index />
    <ChargingItToTheGame />
    <Contact />
  </main>

  <PageFooter />

  <FolioMarginalia />
</BaseLayout>
